U  from now on because sadly William Hurt  the original actor who played him has  passed away he'll appear in Captain  America New World Order and then of  course I'm assuming he will show up in  the Thunderbolts as well I'm assuming  that deal is next to be made especially  considering that it's the very next  movie on The Phase 5 timeline so it  appears that we have our new Thunderbolt  Ross in the MCU and it is Harrison Ford  and he has a long history with Disney  specifically lucasfilm and Star Wars  which is owned by Disney now they are  also doing Indiana Jones as well so this  makes sense he's already a part of  Disney he just got done doing Indiana  Jones 5. he was already working very  close with them and now it looks like  he's going to continue to do so and I'm  excited I love Harrison Ford his  characters have been iconic and I think  he's going to bring a lot to the  character Thunderbolt Ross in the Marvel  Cinematic Universe now moving on to the  new Fantastic Four casting rumors I  gotta say right off the bat I don't know  how I feel about this one so let me know  when you hear these what you think about  them in the comments down below this is  coming from the account demoy and if  you're not familiar with what demoy is  it's basically an account where people  can randomly submit things that they've  heard within the movie industry and some  other Industries as well so do not take  this as a confirmed thing not a  confirmed report just take it as a rumor  for now but this is what the message  says it says Fantastic Four News Maddie  Hassan and Tom Ellis are in the running  for the roles of Sue storm and Reed  Richards and they talk about Johnny and  the thing as well but let's first talk  about these two right here first off  Maddie Hassan admittedly I had never  heard of her before but after doing some  research and watching a few videos of  her I don't think that this would be a  bad choice I think she definitely has a  look to play Sue storm and 